  "details": "Version: 2020.1.1\nDescription of the bug: The stencil buffer used for the eyes, and the stencil buffer visemes used for the mouth of my avatar will suddenly cease to display properly during normal gameplay. Prior to the 2020.1.1 update this could be fixed on a per-client basis by toggling the safety settings, but after the 2020.1.1 update this can only be fixed by resetting VRChat entirely. This bug does not appear to be visually present in unity itself, ONLY inside VRChat. This bug is visible in mirrors, when using Holoport locomotion and when standing outside of the avatar during FBT calibration.\nSteps to reproduce: At this time it is unknown how to force this issue to reproduce manually, but usually it doesn't take long for it to just happen on it's own during normal play.\nAny extra files?: I have provided an image showing what the avatar's eyes and mouth look like normally and after the bug occurs.",
